@@ -40,7 +40,6 @@ safe measurement posture.
 | `GGML_ARIFI_ROCMFPX_FORMATS` (CMake) | **OFF.** Build-time option in `ggml/CMakeLists.txt`, propagated as a PUBLIC compile definition on `ggml-base`. It is deliberately **not** an environment variable: the CPU dot products for these types are entries in `type_traits_cpu[]` (`ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c`), selected at link time, so a runtime toggle could not cover them - the exact defect that made the VNNI slot's first three A/Bs worthless. Two things stay unconditional regardless of the flag: the type-ids in `ggml/include/ggml.h` (the enum is ABI and must not move with a build flag) and `GGML_TYPE_COUNT = 256`. | Compiles the six ROCmFPX serialized weight formats and their whole CPU path: block structs and reference quant/dequant (`ggml/rocmfp4/`, `ggml/rocmfpx/`), `type_traits[]` rows, `type_traits_cpu[]` rows and four scalar `vec_dot`s, the `--check-tensors` row validators in `ggml-quants.c`, six of the seven type-id dispatch sites in `ggml-cpu/ops.cpp`, the `ggml_quantize_chunk` arms, and the llama-side quantizer wiring. Ids adopted verbatim: `100 Q4_0_ROCMFP4` (18 B/32), `101 Q4_0_ROCMFP4_FAST` (17 B/32), `102 Q6_0_ROCMFPX` (26 B/32), `103 Q8_0_ROCMFPX` (33 B/32), `104 Q3_0_ROCMFPX` (14 B/32), `107 Q2_0_ROCMFPX` (10 B/32). It does **not** compile any GPU kernel for these types - Vulkan and CUDA support are separate slots - and it does not port ROCmFPX's quantizer **recipes** (`_LEAN`, `_COHERENT`, `_STRIX`, `_AGENT`), which are a distinct mechanism. | Turn it ON to read or write ROCmFPX GGUFs. On a Vulkan build these types have no GPU pipeline, so `ggml_backend_vk_device_supports_op()` returns false for them and every matmul falls back to CPU - that is why the default is OFF on the 780M, and why Strix Halo / discrete AMD are ON-path only once the HIP and Vulkan slots land. OFF is safe, not lossy: the file is **refused, never guessed at**. | **Correctness proven in both arms on a real artifact. Performance UNMEASURED - no ON/OFF benchmark was run and none should be quoted.**<br><br>**Correction to the slot brief:** it stated there is no ROCmFP-format model on disk and that ON-path execution was therefore likely unverifiable. That is **false**. `<MODELS>/rocmfpx-trial/` holds two native ROCmFP4 GGUFs; `ornith-9b-mtp-kl-Q4_0_ROCMFP4_COHERENT.gguf` was probed directly from its header and carries **257 tensors at type-id 100**, 1 Q6_K and 184 F32, with `general.file_type = 102` and arch `qwen35`. The ON path was verified against it, not by proxy.<br><br>**ON.** llama-server per F-085, `-ngl 0 -c 512`, gate-ON build: the model loaded in **7.0 s**, `/props` reported `model_ftype = Q4_0_ROCMFP4_COHERENT`, and `/completion` on "The capital of France is" returned " Paris." and then repeated the sentence, at **3.24 tok/s** predicted. A chat request produced coherent multi-step reasoning. Execution ran through `rocmfp4_vec_dot_q4_0_q8_0` on CPU, as designed - Vulkan declined the type.<br><br>**OFF.** The identical file on the identical build with the option OFF is refused, verbatim: `gguf_init_from_reader: tensor 'output.weight' of type 100 ((null)) has 4096 elements per row, not a multiple of block size (0)`, then `failed to load model`, exit 1. That is the universal `blck_size == 0` backstop at `ggml/src/gguf.cpp:715`, not new code - which is what makes raising `GGML_TYPE_COUNT` to 256 safe despite the sparse 44..255 range it opens.<br><br>**Reference conformance.** Both ROCmFPX self-test suites were compiled against the ported sources with our own MinGW gcc and pass: `test_rocmfpx.c` (ROCmFP3/6/8 block and row sizes, bpw, mse, imatrix-weighted mse) and `test_rocmfp2_reference.c` (**32520 checks** - layout, packed-byte decode, UE4M3 boundaries, metadata validation, deterministic ties, Python golden vectors, non-finite rejection; fingerprint `78389c1c8a0a57a2`).<br><br>**No regression, OFF arm, same binary.** g128 still works: the native type-43 `Ternary-Bonsai-27B-Abliterated-LowDeg-Q2_0.g128.gguf` loads and answers "The capital of France is" with " Paris." (0.65 tok/s, `-ngl 0`, a 27B fully on CPU under memory pressure). VNNI still works: on `qwen2.5-0.5b-light-q8_0-4xffndownQ2_0-g64.gguf` with `-ngl 0 --no-host -c 1024 -t 8`, `GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK=1` produces `CPU_REPACK model buffer size = 4.68 MiB` with **286** ineligible tensors, and unset produces **no** `CPU_REPACK` line with **290** - reproducing the VNNI row's own documented numbers exactly, with token-identical coherent output in both arms and `CPU_Mapped = 625.75 MiB` in both.<br><br>**Cost of the un-gated part.** `GGML_TYPE_COUNT` 44 -> 256 is paid in both arms. It grows every `[GGML_TYPE_COUNT]`-dimensioned array, of which the Vulkan backend has by far the most (twelve `bool[COUNT]`, five `vk_matmul_pipeline2[COUNT]`, three `vk_pipeline[2][COUNT][8]`). The allocation contract's estimate is ~1.5 KB of `vk_device_struct` per type-id, i.e. **~320 KB more per Vulkan device** - an **estimate carried forward, not a measurement**; `sizeof(vk_matmul_pipeline2)` was not compiled here either. Device init also runs two `for (i = 0; i < GGML_TYPE_COUNT; ++i)` loops (`ggml-vulkan.cpp:4025`, `:6625`) over 256 ids instead of 44; both bodies are trivial, and `ggml_vk_matmul_shmem_support()` was read to confirm it has a `default: break` and performs no type-traits lookup, so an unimplemented id cannot fault it. **Not measured:** device-init wall time before versus after.<br><br>**Known consequence, recorded not fixed.** `tests/test-gguf.cpp` draws random types as `rng() % GGML_TYPE_COUNT` and skips those whose `type_size` is 0. Raising the ceiling to 256 cuts its effective random-type coverage by roughly 5.8x. The test still passes by construction; the coverage loss is real and belongs to whoever next touches that file.<br><br>**Not attempted, named:** GPU kernels for these types (ROCmFPX ships Vulkan dequant shaders and CUDA `mmq`/`mmvq`/`vecdotq`/`fattn` instances; both are separate slots); the ROCmFPX quantizer recipes; a round-trip quantization through our own `llama-quantize` into any of these types; whether `rocmfpx.c`'s 2-bit path is byte-identical to the frozen `rocmfp2_reference.c` (ROCmFPX's own `test_rocmfpx.c` covers only fp3/fp6/fp8); and any perplexity or throughput comparison against `Q4_0` or `Q4_K_M`. Evidence: this row plus the commit trailers on `topic/rocmfp-formats`. |
